  "informal_statement": "# IMO 2026 Problem 5\n\nFind all functions f : ℝ₊ → ℝ₊ such that\n\n    sqrt((x² + f(y)²) / 2)\n      ≥ (f(x) + y) / 2\n      ≥ sqrt(x f(y))\n\nfor all positive x,y.\n\nThe answer is\n\n    f(x) = x + c\n\nfor a constant c ≥ 0.\n\nWe work with `f : ℝ → ℝ` and carry positivity explicitly.\n\nNo `sorry`, `admit`, or additional axioms are used.",
